---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Life in Weeks
permalink: /life-in-weeks/
description: Every week alive, as a little box.
ext_js: [weeks]
---
{#
  Every week between settings.weeks.born and born + settings.weeks.years, one
  box each, grouped into decades. The grid itself comes from _data/weeksGrid.js
  - see that file for why the date arithmetic does not live here.

  Weeks carrying a headline print it and open a detail panel on click; the
  rest are blank squares. assets/ext/js/weeks.js wires up the panel.
#}
<section class="life-in-weeks">
    <p>
        My life, where each week I have been alive is a little box. Inspired by
        <a href="https://waitbutwhy.com/2014/05/life-weeks.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="external-link">this post</a>
        by Tim Urban. When something meaningful happens - for better or for
        worse - I make a note of it in
        <a href="https://github.com/corbtastik/quirky/blob/main/src/_data/life-in-weeks.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="external-link">a data file</a>,
        so I can see how much of a life is shaped by a handful of weeks.
    </p>

    <p>
        {{ weeksGrid.livedWeeks }} weeks lived of {{ weeksGrid.totalWeeks }} drawn,
        starting {{ weeksGrid.bornLabel }}. {{ weeksGrid.birthdayCount }} birthdays,
        {{ weeksGrid.schoolWeeks }} weeks at school across
        {{ weeksGrid.schoolCount }} of them,
        {{ weeksGrid.employedWeeks }} weeks at work across
        {{ weeksGrid.roleCount }} jobs, and {{ weeksGrid.eventCount }} weeks with
        something else worth noting. Click a labelled week to read it.
    </p>

    <div class="weeks-legend">
        <span class="weeks-legend-plain"><i></i> a week</span>
        <span class="weeks-legend-birthday"><i></i> a birthday</span>
        <span class="weeks-legend-school"><i></i> at school</span>
        <span class="weeks-legend-work"><i></i> at work</span>
        <span class="weeks-legend-both"><i></i> both</span>
        <span class="weeks-legend-job"><i></i> a job started</span>
        <span class="weeks-legend-event"><i></i> something happened</span>
        <span class="weeks-legend-future"><i></i> not yet</span>
    </div>

    {%- for decade in weeksGrid.decades %}
    <div class="weeks-decade">
        <h2 class="weeks-decade-title">{{ decade.label }}</h2>
        <div class="weeks-row">
            <div class="week-age">{{ decade.ageLabel }}</div>
            {#- `classes` and `title` are assembled in _data/weeksGrid.js: a week
                can be a life event, the start of a job, employment, a birthday
                and still to come, all at once. -#}
            {%- for week in decade.weeks %}
            {%- if week.headline %}
            <button type="button"
                    class="{{ week.classes }}"
                    data-date="{{ week.date }}"
                    data-date-label="{{ week.dateLabel }}"
                    data-headline="{{ week.headline }}"
                    data-description="{{ week.description }}"
                    title="{{ week.title }}">{{ week.headline }}</button>
            {%- else %}
            <div class="{{ week.classes }}" title="{{ week.title }}"></div>
            {%- endif %}
            {%- endfor %}
        </div>
    </div>
    {%- endfor %}
</section>

{#- One detail panel, reused by whichever week was clicked. A popover per week
    would mean several thousand of them in the document. -#}
<div id="weeks-detail" class="weeks-detail" hidden role="dialog" aria-live="polite" aria-labelledby="weeks-detail-headline">
    <button type="button" class="weeks-detail-close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <h3 id="weeks-detail-headline"></h3>
    <p class="weeks-detail-date"></p>
    <p class="weeks-detail-description"></p>
</div>
